@page "/components/dot-pattern"

<PageTitle>DotPattern — Unpoly.Blazor.Shadcn</PageTitle>

<h1 class="doc-h1">DotPattern</h1>
<p class="doc-lede">
    A decorative lattice of dots — the same absolute overlay as <code>GridPattern</code>, drawn with
    circles instead of lines. Pure SVG, no JS.
</p>

<h2 class="doc-h2">Basic</h2>
<Example Source="DotPatternExample.razor"><DotPatternExample /></Example>

<h2 class="doc-h2">When not to use it</h2>
<p class="doc-note">
    The dots carry no information: the overlay is <code>aria-hidden</code> and
    <code>pointer-events-none</code>, so nothing on top of it is announced and nothing behind it
    steals a click. Never let the pattern be the only thing marking a boundary — a row of dots that
    disappears at high zoom is not a divider. Use <code>Separator</code> for a rule, and
    <code>Chart</code> when the marks are data.
</p>
